# Alignment-threshold diagnostic (td-4e19d.28) — artifact policy.
#
# COMMITTED: alignment_threshold_diagnostic.tsv — one row per
# (cell, min_identity), the table that separates a QUAST scoring-threshold
# effect from a genuinely non-reconstructing assembly.
#
# IGNORED: the per-cell, per-threshold QUAST output trees. Each censored cell is
# rescored at four identity thresholds, so this directory holds 4 full QUAST
# runs per cell; all of it is regenerable from the committed sweep checkpoints
# by re-running benchmarking/ont_alignment_threshold_diagnostic.jl.
#
# The glob was `Lambda__*/` only, which left a T4 rescore tree tracked —
# and the committed table carries 48 T4 rows, so those trees are produced by
# an ordinary run. Match on the cell-id shape instead of one organism, so a
# third organism cannot reintroduce the omission.
*__*x__seed*/

# In-flight temps from publish_atomically — a partial write, not a backup.
*.tsv.tmp.*
